// `namespace` declares the file's module path; `use` imports names in both the single form
// (`App.Models.User`) and the grouped form (`App.Billing.{Invoice, Receipt}`), each resolving to a
// real declaration in a sibling module that the linker merges in.
//
// This was an M0 fixture asserting the opposite: back then an imported name resolved to an opaque
// STUB, so `User { ... }` constructed something with no declaration behind it. Module loading has
// since landed (E0019 for an unresolved import), which made the M0 form uncompilable — but it kept
// passing, because the single-file harness path checked the raw text without ever running the
// linker. Giving it the modules it imports is what makes the case test the language as it is.
// expect: stdout "Ada"
// expect: stdout "42"
// expect: stdout "true"
// expect: exit 0
namespace App.Orders;

use App.Models.User;
use App.Billing.{Invoice, Receipt};

customer = User { name: "Ada", id: 7 };
invoice = Invoice { number: 42, paid: true };

echo customer.name;
echo invoice.number;
echo invoice.paid;
